{"page_content": "5.1\nExperiment Requirements\nFLEX-2\nSRD Rev. 1\nHardware Requirements (cont.)\nSection\nDescription\nRequirements\n5.1.3\nInitial Pressure\n- test pressures at 0.5, 1.0, 2.0 and 3.0 atm \u00b1 0.05\natm\n- chamber pressure to be maintained within \u00b1 10% of\ninitial pressure throughout each test\n5.1.4\nInitial Ambient\n- mole fractions of O2 from 0.10 to 0.40\n- diluents will be either N2 or He\n- initial gas temperature at 18 oC \u221227 oC\n- humidity < 10% for all test points\n- quiescent atmosphere prior to ignition\n- well-mixed gases prior to ignition\n5.1.5\nDroplet\nTranslation\n- tethered droplet velocities between 0.1 cm/sec and\n5.0 cm/sec \u00b1 1%\n- tethered dropelt acceleration/deceleration shall be\ncontrollable\n5.1.6\nOperational\nRequirements\n- allow at least 2 minutes after \ufb01lling chamber to\nensure gas temperature and pressure has stabilized\n- allow a \u2018droplet dwell time\u2019 of at least 10 sec to\nensure all droplet motion imparted by droplet\ndeployment and needle retraction has subsided\n- a \u2018near real time\u2019 downlink of the color camera\nvideo and the chamber gas pressure and\ntemperature shall be provided\n- fuel vapor mole fraction of < 0.005 in the\natmosphere\n- mole fraction of product species from previous tests\nshall be < 0.02 (for each product species; e.g., CO,\nCO2 , H2O)\n32", "metadata": {"source": "FLEX-2 SRD Final.pdf", "page": 38}}